{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/946577-how-does-the-solar-dodge-inititative-reactor-work-3e","id":946577,"title":"How does the Solar Dodge Inititative Reactor work? [3e]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-08T17:42:49-07:00","id":946577,"title":"How does the Solar Dodge Inititative Reactor work? [3e]","content":"I've heard before that Solar Dodge allows a person to play someone who just dodges everything and can build init quickly without ever needing to attack, but, whenever I look at the charms, it seems like you're only ever getting 1i or 2i at a time. Is the assumption that you're evading large groups or what? How does it work? What charms do you need?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T18:09:35-07:00","id":946594,"title":"","content":"Seven Shadows Evasion + Refinement of Flowing Shadows gives you init every round as long as you stay within Medium range and don't get hit.<br /> <br /> Unbowed Willow Meditation takes all of your foes Initiative and Crashes them if they miss with a Decisive and you don't use Charms to boost your evasion (and Drifting Leaf Elusion and Rumour of Form don't count as charms thanks to Way of Whispers technique).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T18:50:11-07:00","id":946636,"title":"","content":"<b>Quickly</b>, not so much, unless you are willing to take some risks with Unbowed Willow Meditation. Or evading multiple foes, sure. But playing it safe one on one? Yeah, it is gonna take a while to build up a lot of Initiative with Dodge.<br /> <br /> Personally, I wouldn't really try using only that. It is a great boon to get some Init even when defending, but against a dangerous enemy who can actually hit you every now and then with a withering attack you are not gonna stay ahead using only the Init trickle from Dodge, and you probably don't wanna risk defending against a decisive with only DLE and RoF.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T19:04:03-07:00","id":946649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/946577-how-does-the-solar-dodge-inititative-reactor-work-3e?p=946636#post946636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Quickly</b>, not so much, unless you are willing to take some risks with Unbowed Willow Meditation. Or evading multiple foes, sure. But playing it safe one on one? Yeah, it is gonna take a while to build up a lot of Initiative with Dodge.<br /> <br /> Personally, I wouldn't really try using only that. It is a great boon to get some Init even when defending, but against a dangerous enemy who can actually hit you every now and then with a withering attack you are not gonna stay ahead using only the Init trickle from Dodge, and you probably don't wanna risk defending against a decisive with only DLE and RoF.</div> </div> </div> </div>Danelsan speaks the truth. Dodge is great if you already have a kick-ass way of attacking, just by itself, it kind of is like Resistance in that it is a very passive charmset.<br /> <br /> prototype00","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T20:05:23-07:00","id":946697,"title":"","content":"&lt;&lt;&lt;Wants to make Dodge Supernal Night Caste now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9039-heartwood-jack","name":"Heartwood Jack","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9039_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T20:27:51-07:00","id":946707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heartwood Jack</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/946577-how-does-the-solar-dodge-inititative-reactor-work-3e?p=946697#post946697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&lt;&lt;&lt;Wants to make Dodge Supernal Night Caste now <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I've been knocking around the idea with some of the items I've been making lately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T01:33:26-07:00","id":946807,"title":"","content":"Dodge Mote Generation...<br /> <br /> <b>Charms of importance:</b><br /> Flow Like Blood<br /> -This removes all the penalties you could ever take, and gives you 1 free initiative point if staying close to the enemy. It also reduces the cost of Reed in the Wind to 1 initiative.<br /> <br /> Quick Silver Feint + Force Stealing Feint<br /> -This steals 1 point of initiative each time you are missed. <br /> <br /> Thousand Step's Stillness<br /> -This lets you gain 1 point of initiative per 1 or 2 they rolled, since they are likely trying to throw as many dice at you as possible, although you probably should combo this with Hundred Shadow Ways to have become immune to Excellent Strike like effects. <br /> <br /> <b>Full Effect:</b><br /> Basically if you are willing to be careful on offense motes since you will be regenerating none due to expenses, you will be likely gaining 5 or more initiative just from dodging.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1635-citadel97501","name":"Citadel97501","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"544"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T22:31:40-07:00","id":948381,"title":"","content":"So after some looking at the Dodge charms, I've come up with the following list of all the Init modding Solar Dodge Charms:<br /> <br /> Shadow Dancer Method (D5, E1, Permanent) - for 1m you can ignore the 2i cost when Disengaging. If an opponent approaches you and you move away, but opt to close with them on your next move, you gain 2i.<br /> <br /> <b>Searing Quicksilver Flight</b> (D4, E1, Permanent) and <b>Force-Stealing Feint</b> (D5, E2, Permanent) - Whenever you successfully dodge an attack, your opponent loses one additional init. With Force-Stealing Feint you gain the lost init.<br /> <br /> Safety Between Heartbeats (D5, E2, Reflexive) - After you successfully dodge an attack, you can pay 5m to cause your opponent to lose 1i for every 1 they rolled on the attack.<br /> <br /> <b>Flow Like Blood</b> (D4, E2, Reflexive) - For 5m, 1w you gain several benefits for the scene, including +1i each round you remain within close range of an enemy without being successfully attacked.<br /> <br /> <b>Thousand Steps' Stillness</b> (D5, E3, Reflexive) - After successfully dodging an attack, you may pay 5m to gain 1i per 1 or 2 rolled on the attack roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Unbowed Willow Meditation</b> (D5, E3, Permanent) - If you successfully dodge a Decisive Attack without using a charm, you steal all the attackers init and crash them. Way of Whispers Technique synergizes well with this charm.<br /> <br /> Unbridled Shade Attitude (D5, E3, Permanent) - Gain 1i for every -0 HL damaged by a Decisive Attack. This one is really just there to help recoup the losses from Living Bonds Unburdened, but you might be rocking 3x Ox Bodies, I dunno.<br /> <br /> Refinement of Flowing Shadows (D5, E5, Permanent) - After you use Seven Shadow Evasion to dodge something, you gain 1i and 1i every round until the next time you get hit.<br /> <br /> <br /> From looking at all of these, I've come to a few conclusions:<br /> <br /> 1) All of these charms are either Permanent or specifically say that they can only be used after you successfully dodge. As such, none of them need to be declared when you're declaring your defense charms beforehand. So, there's no real downside from having them, except for the points you spent to get the charms.<br /> <br /> 2) Shadow Dancer Method is the only charm that gains you init at E1 and only 2i per turn, so, if you want to have the &quot;Evade Opponent until you Strike!&quot; thing going on, you'll need to take Dodge Supernal, or build up to it over the course of the game. The charms in Bold above are the ones I'd consider best for this style of fighting (though keep in mind I've never tried playing this type of character, so I might well be mistaken). <br /> <br /> Those charms together mean you get 1i every round, 1i every time you dodge successfully and you can pay 5m to get additional init equal to the 1&amp;2s on the attack roll or, if you didn't need a charm to defend, you get all the opponent's init and crash them. While you'd probably get more init with a weapon, these don't have to be mutually exclusive options. With prereqs, it costs 9 of your starting 15 charms, and you might want a couple more just to ensure you can evade everything, but it's doable at chargen.<br /> <br /> Note that, to gain anything but the 1i from FLB each action, you need to be attacked, so these charms don't combine well with Stealth charms. As several of them key off you remaining in close range to an opponent, they don't really combine well with Archery either. Thrown, Melee, or MA would seem to be your best options for other charms to use with this set up. MA especially, as several of them combine well with Dodge like Snake (gives bonuses to Evasion, needs high init), Black Claw (Evasion Bonus, steal init, attack penalties), and Dreaming Pearl (Evasion bonuses, can steal init).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T04:17:56-07:00","id":948501,"title":"","content":"Isnt there a charm that lets you defend other with dodge?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Nope. I was thinking of the agata. Pitty,thats what Dodge is really missing... probably for balance purposes.<br /> <br /> That said, Dodge and Resistancr share the same issue. Sure YOU are basically immortal or unattackable, but the rest of your circle isnt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 08-11-2016, 08:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T06:02:05-07:00","id":948546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/946577-how-does-the-solar-dodge-inititative-reactor-work-3e?p=948501#post948501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isnt there a charm that lets you defend other with dodge?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Nope. I was thinking of the agata. Pitty,thats what Dodge is really missing... probably for balance purposes.<br /> <br /> That said, Dodge and Resistancr share the same issue. Sure YOU are basically immortal or unattackable, but the rest of your circle isnt.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see such a charm working with Resistance (there is fun potential in being the guy who puts his body between the blow and the target). Dodge... less so. I can't see how that would work*, and it's just... less in-theme.<br /> <br /> *I mean, I guess you could carry your ally away? but that would either look stupid in some situation, or come with pretty big caveats and pitfalls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T07:06:27-07:00","id":948574,"title":"","content":"The dodge initiative generation is also compatible with use of the Performance buff songs, giving you a way to stay out of crash despite being unable to attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5376-atg","name":"AtG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5376_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"691"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T07:08:51-07:00","id":948576,"title":"","content":"I wonder, what does it look like when a Sid Defend Other with Trouble Reduction Strategy ? Pushing them out of harm way ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T07:26:32-07:00","id":948588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/946577-how-does-the-solar-dodge-inititative-reactor-work-3e?p=948576#post948576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder, what does it look like when a Sid Defend Other with Trouble Reduction Strategy ? Pushing them out of harm way ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereals being what they are...I sincerely doubt it is that simple.<br /> <br /> The phrasing of the text makes it look like what they are actually doing is executing the Dodge Charm, but making it so that some other person actually gets the benefits of it. More likely, it looks like the Sidereal doing some weird thing...then all of a sudden their buddy moves as if they had used a Sidereal Dodge Charm.<br /> <br /> So, for example...a Siddie using Trouble Reduction Strategy to apply Duck Fate on behalf of a friend would probably look like the Siddie doing some weird Shenanigans and then their friend reflexively Ducks Fate...which in my head, looks something like &quot;I saw you get hit by that sword...you saw you get hit by that sword...everyone saw you get hit by that sword. But there's no blood or bruises or other injuries because I missed.&quot;<br /> <br /> Alternatively, a Siddie using TRS to apply Avoidance Kata to a friend would basically look like that friend winking out of the scene just like the Sidereal would have if they used it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3937-guildsbounty","name":"guildsbounty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T07:33:52-07:00","id":948595,"title":"","content":"Oooh, I'm talking about the 2.5 version of the Charm actually, it lets Defend Other using your Dodge instead of Parry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T11:59:40-07:00","id":948724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/946577-how-does-the-solar-dodge-inititative-reactor-work-3e?p=948381#post948381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unbridled Shade Attitude (D5, E3, Permanent) - Gain 1i for every -0 HL damaged by a Decisive Attack. This one is really just there to help recoup the losses from Living Bonds Unburdened, but you might be rocking 3x Ox Bodies, I dunno.</div> </div> </div> </div>It combines well with a pile of 5 Stamina Ox-Bodies, but where it really shines is in combination with effects that give a bunch of -0 HLs like Feit of Imparted Nature or Iron Skin Concentration. They also substantially enhance its prerequisite. Having to deal 10+ damage to avoid being crashed really puts a damper on decisive flurries.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10881-anasurimbor","name":"Anasurimbor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T12:55:07-07:00","id":948774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LeTipex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/946577-how-does-the-solar-dodge-inititative-reactor-work-3e?p=948546#post948546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see such a charm working with Resistance (there is fun potential in being the guy who puts his body between the blow and the target). Dodge... less so. I can't see how that would work*, and it's just... less in-theme.<br /> <br /> *I mean, I guess you could carry your ally away? but that would either look stupid in some situation, or come with pretty big caveats and pitfalls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't a &quot;Dodge Defend Other&quot; action simply involve the Dodge character pushing the target out of the way before an axe goes through their skull, or yanking them down the instant before an arrow thrums through the air where they were standing? You see that sort of thing quite often in movies and such, but it doesn't really work with Parry where you're actually using your weapon to block an oncoming attack rather than helping your buddy avoid the attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T12:55:07-07:00","id":948775,"title":"","content":"*EDITED* Got a double post for some reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T14:57:57-07:00","id":948878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AtG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/946577-how-does-the-solar-dodge-inititative-reactor-work-3e?p=948574#post948574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The dodge initiative generation is also compatible with use of the Performance buff songs, giving you a way to stay out of crash despite being unable to attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Welp, stealin' this for one of my important NPC's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10291-zeesun","name":"Zeesun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"252"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T17:35:08-07:00","id":948959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AtG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/946577-how-does-the-solar-dodge-inititative-reactor-work-3e?p=948574#post948574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The dodge initiative generation is also compatible with use of the Performance buff songs, giving you a way to stay out of crash despite being unable to attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively, songs from Silver-Voiced Nightingale Style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T19:49:15-07:00","id":949037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/946577-how-does-the-solar-dodge-inititative-reactor-work-3e?p=948959#post948959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Alternatively, songs from Silver-Voiced Nightingale Style.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but there is no really notable synergy there beyond the fact that SVNS uses dodge-based defense. The reason Performance buff songs are notable is that they don't allow you to take non-reflexive actions, which normally locks you out of initiative generation entirely.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, Solar Dodge and Silver-Voiced Nightingale are two great tastes that taste great together, there's just nothing in particular about passive initiative gen that SVNS loves.","